Subject: Re: PayNet discovery recap: tool definitions, routing, and next steps

Sam, Emily — thanks for the quick note. See inline answers + an SDK snippet below. I also attached a clearer example manifest and the sample prompts file.

Auth / SDK: the Redwood SDK supports both API-key and OIDC flows. For OIDC we provide a token exchange endpoint in the private control plane; SDK exposes an auth helper that will fetch and rotate short-lived tokens. For a POC you can set a scoped API key in environment variables.

Fallback semantics: yes — tool semantics are preserved. A model variant that lacks capability will return a standardized "fallback_action" with a confidence flag; the runtime will either run the alternative model or call configured fallback handlers. For the deterministic billing ops we recommend forcing sequential execution and an idempotency_key on side-effecting calls.

Rerank vs latency: recommended flow to hit p95:
- Embedding index (ANN) shortlist top 50 in ~10–30ms depending on index;
- Cross-encoder re-rank top 5–10 which adds ~30–60ms depending on model size.
- Total additional latency can stay within your p95 if embeddings lookup is colocated and we parallelize non-blocking lookups.

SDK snippet (pseudo-JS):
const rdw = require('@redwood/inference');
const client = rdw.init({ authMethod: 'oidc' /* or api_key */ });

// Parallel read-only lookups
const [profile, catalog, kbResults] = await Promise.all([
  client.callTool('getCustomerProfile', { id }),
  client.callTool('productCatalog', { sku }),
  client.callTool('kbSearch', { query })
]);

// Generate action (structured)
const actionResp = await client.generate({
  model: 'redwood-structured-v2',
  input: { profile, catalog, kbResults },
  outputSchema: 'action_envelope_v1'
});

// Guarded side-effect (sequential)
if (actionResp.action && actionResp.action.side_effect === true) {
  await client.callTool('applyRefund', { ...actionResp.action.args, idempotency_key: actionResp.request_id });
}

Tool manifest example (excerpt - see attached YAML):
- name: getCustomerProfile
  side_effect: false
  input_schema: { id: 'string' }
  rate_limit_per_min: 300
- name: applyRefund
  side_effect: true
  input_schema: { account_id: 'string', amount: 'number' }
  idempotency_key: true
  retry_policy: { on: '5xx', attempts: 3, backoff: 'exponential' }

Error handling summary:
- 4xx from tool: surface to model as deterministic failure; do not retry automatically.
- 5xx / transient: client retry with exponential backoff.
- Circuit breaker: enforce a short-term circuit if >X 5xxs in rolling window.
- Idempotency: require idempotency_key for all side-effecting operations to allow safe retries.

